<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kieu Cong Tien</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 938</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Kiều Công Tiễn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kieu Cong Tien was a Vietnamese commander who in 937 murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duong-dinh-nghe">Duong Dinh Nghe</a>, the governor of the Tinh Hai circuit who had expelled the Southern Han, and took power himself. Facing a campaign of revenge by Nghe's son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-quyen">Ngo Quyen</a>, he appealed to the Southern Han for help, but Ngo Quyen killed him in 938 and then defeated the Han fleet at the Battle of Bach Dang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kieu-cong-tien.jpg" alt="Kieu Cong Tien" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hoàng Hữu Xứng (1831-1905) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VietNamToanCanhDuDo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
